From 463b4ccbc3f23702b5bfc622c722386f6a1e6996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:23:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 74/91] feat(visualizer): bring the Hanabi lyric style over
 from upstream v0.7.22

- hanabi/: 26 files taken verbatim from the v0.7.22 tag (scene, MG ornaments,
  fireworks, collage, per-character colour blocks, shot transitions)
- pixi/: the upstream 0.7.21 directory move, done as forwarding shims for the
  three modules we already have (and already patched), so both paths resolve
  to one implementation; pixiProgramLinks / pixiWebGLContext / bloomFilter are
  taken as-is
- visualizer/tuningDefinition.ts: a subset (numberWithin + defineVisualizerTuning)
  because upstream generalised the whole tuning contract in 0.7.21 and this
  branch still runs on tuningRegistry
- services/beatFx/: inert stand-ins. Upstream's beat analysis (services/analysis)
  arrived after this branch; every beat-driven path in Hanabi gates on
  isBeatFxReady(), so the style renders exactly as if smart-beat were off
- settings panel and quick controls are left out of this step: they need
  upstream's settings kit; the style itself is untouched
- definition.ts: optional glyph / command / beatEffects / renderQuickControls /
  ownFontSizeNoticeKey fields, all additive
- motionSignals: beatImpact / downbeatImpact as zero signals

Verified on the device (SCA-AL00): style renders full screen, shot transitions,
colour blocks and ornaments all animate.
